.TH PKGADD 1 "2026-09-07" "@PROJECT_NAME@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pkgadd \- install an Emerald package archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkgadd
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ package.epkg.tar.xz ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkgadd
installs an epkg package archive and updates the package database. It may upgrade or reinstall an existing package. System installation requires root privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -u, --upgrade
Upgrade an installed package.
.TP
.B -r, --reinstall
Reinstall an installed package.
.TP
.B -c, --ignore-conflict
Ignore package file conflicts.
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Print installed files.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help.
.TP
.B --no-backup
Do not back up configuration files during an upgrade.
.TP
.B --print-db-dir
Print the package database directory and exit.
.TP
.B --root=PATH
Install into PATH instead of the system root.
.SH FILES
The package database location is determined by Emerald's package metadata and can be queried with \fB--print-db-dir\fR. Configuration files may receive the configured \fB.@EPKGNEW_EXT@\fR suffix during upgrades.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; non-zero on invalid archives, conflicts, missing dependencies, permission errors, or installation failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkgbuild (1),
.BR pkgdel (1),
.BR @PROJECT_NAME@ (1)
